---
title: Consistent asset batch
description: Prepare one generation request from several references and named outputs.
schema:
  Reference:
    id: string
    url: ["string.url", "@", { description: "The supplied artifact's image URL." }]
    role: "'identity' | 'materials' | 'construction'"
    instruction: string
  Output:
    name: string
    view: string
    purpose: string
    requirements: string[]
  Batch:
    subject: string
    references: Reference[]
    outputs: Output[]
    invariants: string[]
    guide: ["boolean", "@", { default: false }]
input: Batch
---
# Generate a coherent asset set

Subject: **{subject}**.

Treat this as one coordinated request. The outputs represent the same subject.
Use each supplied reference only for the role and instruction assigned to it.

## Reference responsibilities

<$each items={references} as="reference">
  ### {reference.id} — {reference.role}

  Source: {reference.url}

  {reference.instruction}

</$each>
## What must remain consistent

<$each items={invariants} as="invariant">
  - {invariant}
</$each>

## Required outputs

<$each items={outputs} as="output">
  ### {output.name}

  View: {output.view}.

  Downstream use: {output.purpose}

  <$each items={output.requirements} as="requirement">
    - {requirement}
  </$each>

</$each>
<$show if={guide}>
  The attached guide defines the output regions. Match the region labels to the
  output names above. Preserve the guide's borders and keep each subject inside
  its assigned region.

</$show>
<$show if={!guide}>
  Return each named output as a separate image, using the same framing scale.

</$show>
<$include src="./shared/consistency.mdt" />
